{
  "mn148:0.1": "Middle Discourses 148 ",
  "mn148:0.2": "Six By Six ",
  "mn148:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "mn148:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Sāvatthī in Jeta’s Grove, Anāthapiṇḍika’s monastery. ",
  "mn148:1.3": "There the Buddha addressed the mendicants, ",
  "mn148:1.4": "“Mendicants!” ",
  "mn148:1.5": "“Venerable sir,” they replied. ",
  "mn148:1.6": "The Buddha said this: ",
  "mn148:2.1": "“Mendicants, I shall teach you the Dhamma that’s good in the beginning, good in the middle, and good in the end, meaningful and well-phrased. And I shall reveal a spiritual practice that’s entirely full and pure, namely, ",
  "mn148:2.2": "the six sets of six. ",
  "mn148:2.3": "Listen and apply your mind well, I will speak.” ",
  "mn148:2.4": "“Yes, sir,” they replied. ",
  "mn148:2.5": "The Buddha said this: ",
  "mn148:3.1": "“The six interior sense fields should be understood. The six exterior sense fields should be understood. The six classes of consciousness should be understood. The six classes of contact should be understood. The six classes of feeling should be understood. The six classes of craving should be understood. ",
  "mn148:4.1": "‘The six interior sense fields should be understood.’ ",
  "mn148:4.2": "That’s what I said, but why did I say it? ",
  "mn148:4.3": "There are the sense fields of the eye, ear, nose, tongue, body, and mind. ",
  "mn148:4.4": "‘The six interior sense fields should be understood.’ ",
